WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.200
At night a lighthouse doesn’t tell you its name.

2
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:06.225
It tells you its rhythm, and you look it up.

3
00:00:06.475 --> 00:00:09.500
That rhythm is called the light’s characteristic.

4
00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:11.975
Look at the patterns on screen.

5
00:00:12.225 --> 00:00:14.200
Fixed is a steady light.

6
00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:17.575
Flashing means it’s dark longer than it’s lit.

7
00:00:17.825 --> 00:00:20.600
Quick is about sixty flashes a minute.

8
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:23.650
Isophase means equal light and dark.

9
00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:29.375
Occulting is the reverse of flashing: lit longer than dark, with short eclipses.

10
00:00:29.625 --> 00:00:32.725
Group flashing shows its flashes in groups.

11
00:00:32.975 --> 00:00:35.550
And Morse A is a short and a long.

12
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.100
Now read a chart label with me.

13
00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:42.825
F L two, white, ten seconds, forty-five feet, fourteen miles.

14
00:00:43.075 --> 00:00:44.675
What does it say?

15
00:00:45.675 --> 00:00:55.000
A white light, flashing in groups of two, every ten seconds, forty-five feet above mean high water, with a nominal range of fourteen miles.

16
00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:58.650
So when you think you’ve found your light, time it with a watch.

17
00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:01.325
The period will tell you if you’re right.
